HOW THE FILES ARE COPIED
------------------------

scripts/vendor-ai-elements.mjs copies each file below from an ai-elements checkout. The bytes are
upstream's; the one change is the import alias the CLI also rewrites:

  @repo/shadcn-ui/components/ui/<x>  ->  @/components/ui/<x>
  @repo/shadcn-ui/lib/utils          ->  @/lib/utils

Each FILE row names the upstream path and the sha256 of the UPSTREAM bytes.
tests/ai-elements-provenance.test.mjs reverses the alias on every local copy and checks the result
hashes to its row, so no local edit to a vendored file goes unrecorded. Everything else the
components import (radix-ui, lucide-react, streamdown, shiki, motion, use-stick-to-bottom, …) is an
npm dependency in apps/web/package.json, not a stand-in.

The styling is upstream's Tailwind classes, compiled by Tailwind CSS v4 from src/styles/ai-elements.css,
which also holds the theme tokens (the app's own palette) and the scoped preflight.

