VENDOR MARKS (components/ai-elements/logos)
-------------------------------------------

The model picker's vendor marks are lobehub's monochrome icons, vendored byte for byte:

  package: @lobehub/icons-static-svg 1.95.1 (npm), fetched from cdn.jsdelivr.net
  project: https://github.com/lobehub/lobe-icons
  licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2023 LobeHub. The npm package ships no licence file, so logos/LICENSE
           is the repository's own, from
           https://raw.githubusercontent.com/lobehub/lobe-icons/2e76c48721e91b9aaa40803a0fa2eb8aca7399c4/LICENSE
           sha256: add9d7531d1b21646317a8958e38fc727506fa39d24bdecb44154d943c82753a

Each file is one <path> on a 24x24 viewBox in currentColor, with no script, no link and no event
attribute. logos/marks.ts is GENERATED from them (title, viewBox, path data) so nothing is ever set as
HTML; tests/model-logos.test.mjs re-derives it from the files and checks every hash below.

The marks are trademarks of their owners. The licence covers the drawings, not the marks; each one is
shown only beside that owner's own model, to say whose model it is.

Deliberately not vendored: poolside.svg (its mark is a gradient drawn with masks and ids, which breaks
the one-colour rule and could collide with ids elsewhere on the page); Nex AGI and Thinking Machines
have no mark in the set. Those three get their initial in a disc — nobody's logo is drawn for them.

