NOT VENDORED, AND WHY (upstream packages/elements/src at the same commit)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Checked against the product's real surfaces on 2026-09-23. Each is one line: what it is, why not now.

  plan               A Plan-mode card with its step list. The owner's D-UX-2 keeps plan checklists
                     out of the conversation; the next step is one row inside Thinking and the plan
                     itself is under Details. Needs ui/card, which is not vendored.
  checkpoint         "Saved point · Restore" after a turn. The workspace's restore lives in the
                     checkpoints drawer and lib/undo.ts; a second restore control per turn is a new
                     feature, not a swap of a lookalike.
  context            A usage ring over tokens (tokenlens). Credits are settled by the worker per run
                     and shown from its own figure; a client-side token estimate would be a second,
                     disagreeing number.
  environment-variables
                     Built to reveal and copy secret values (EyeIcon, CopyButton, ui/switch). The
                     browser never has a model key — only its last four characters — so a component
                     whose purpose is showing the value has nothing to show. Settings › Models & keys
                     is a plain list instead.
  confirmation, question, queue
                     Each needs a worker round-trip that does not exist yet (tool approval, ask_user,
                     a queued-message store).
  image              Re-implemented, no upstream copy kept: image.tsx renders the
                     Branding window's composed icon and thumbnails. Chat images below still use
                     SafeImage.
  artifact, audio-player
                     Generated images and sounds already render through lib/generative-ui (SafeImage,
                     SafeAudio: fetched with the person's token, with loading and gone states). A swap
                     is only safe with those states kept, and is left for its own change.
  speech-input, mic-selector, transcription, voice-selector
                     No voice input or spoken reply exists in the product.
  file-tree, snippet, inline-citation, test-results, stack-trace
                     Their surfaces (files panel, pairing code, Plan-mode citations, playtest checks,
                     Luau errors) work today as they are; each swap is its own reviewable change.
  agent, commit, sandbox, terminal, schema-display, package-info, jsx-preview, open-in-chat,
  web-preview, persona, canvas, node, edge, connection, controls, panel, toolbar
                     Developer surfaces (tool schemas, git, terminals, npm), model-written JSX run in
                     our origin (jsx-preview), handing the prompt to another product (open-in-chat),
                     an iframe previewer for URLs (a Roblox place is not one), a Rive mascot (the
                     mascot is cancelled), and @xyflow/react graphs (not installable here).

  Vendored and now unused: task.tsx. Its one surface was the planned-steps checklist inside Thinking,
  which D-UX-2 removed. It is kept, with its row above, so the row and the copy stay checkable if it
  returns.
